181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (The Linux Service and Process Supervisor is a C-based project used to manage multiple services running on a Linux system. It helps in starting services and continuously monitoring their processes while they are running. If a service stops or crashes, the supervisor detects it and can restart the service according to the restart limit given in the configuration file.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 131 0 R
/E (The project also provides a command-line tool called svctl, through which the user can start, stop, restart, pause, resume, and check the status of services. Communication between svctl and the main supervisor is handled using named FIFO. The project uses important Linux concepts such as fork\(\), execv\(\), waitpid\(\), signals, process control, and inter-process communication. It provides a practical way to understand how processes and services can be managed in Linux.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
